@title Tallgrass Telemetry Pipeline
@subtitle Architecture for the control room
@author Asset Performance team
@date 2026-10-06

Owned by Asset Performance. Reviewed 2026-10-06.

## Overview
Turbine data is collected on site and summarized before it is sent over a limited link. The grid operator receives output and availability figures directly from the site.

## Pipeline
diagram telem dir=LR title="Telemetry pipeline"
telem: turbines "Turbine Controllers" svc "62 turbines"
telem: scada "Site SCADA" svc
telem: hist "Edge Historian" store
telem: ingest "Ingest Gateway" svc
telem: tsdb "Time-Series Store" db
telem: fc "Forecast Service" svc
telem: grid "Grid Operator" ext
telem: room "Control Room" user "tablets" focus
telem: turbines -> scada : 1 sample per second
telem: scada -> hist : buffered storage
telem: scada -> grid : output and availability, every 4 seconds
telem: hist -> ingest : compressed batches
telem: ingest -> tsdb : validated samples
telem: tsdb -> fc : history
telem: fc -> room : 24 hour output forecast
telem: tsdb -> room : live and historical views
telem: group site "Tallgrass Site" turbines, scada, hist
telem: group cloud "Windspire Operations Cloud" ingest, tsdb, fc

!! On satellite fallback, the Control Room sees one-minute averages, not full-resolution data.
! The Edge Historian can hold 72 hours of full-resolution data until the fiber link returns.

## Sizing
- 62 turbines with 140 signals each make 8680 samples per second, or about 750 million samples a day.
- Full-resolution data is kept 30 days. One-minute averages are kept 5 years.
- The fiber link is 100 Mbps. The satellite fallback is 2 Mbps and can carry one-minute averages only.
